From 62775be151bacd5bbbea640f5f73601413ca6a96 Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: "David C. Manuelda" <StormByte@gmail.com>
Date: Mon, 2 Nov 2026 04:55:44 +0100
Subject: [PATCH] libvmaf/adm_avx2: handle small coefficients before clz and
 rounding shifts

The AVX2 decoupling loop calls get_best15_from32() for every lane before
blending the result with the unshifted small coefficients. Unlike the
scalar call sites, it does not restrict calls to values >= 32768.
Zero therefore reaches __builtin_clz(), and small nonzero values can
produce a negative rounding shift.

Return small inputs unchanged with a zero shift before computing clz.
This matches the scalar branch and initializes both outputs for all
lanes without changing the large-coefficient rounding path.

Reproduced with UBSan during existing integer ADM/VMAF pipeline tests.
---
 libvmaf/src/feature/x86/adm_avx2.c | 4 ++++
 1 file changed, 4 insertions(+)

diff --git a/libvmaf/src/feature/x86/adm_avx2.c b/libvmaf/src/feature/x86/adm_avx2.c
index 27ba2148..dd8d400d 100644
--- a/libvmaf/src/feature/x86/adm_avx2.c
+++ b/libvmaf/src/feature/x86/adm_avx2.c
@@ -1345,6 +1345,10 @@ void adm_dwt2_8_avx2(const uint8_t *src, const adm_dwt_band_t *dst,
 
 static inline uint16_t get_best15_from32(uint32_t temp, int *x)
 {
+    if (temp < 32768) {
+        *x = 0;
+        return temp;
+    }
     int k = __builtin_clz(temp);    //built in for intel
     k = 17 - k;
     temp = (temp + (1 << (k - 1))) >> k;
-- 
2.56.0

